      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-10-14_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>TOO MUCH LIGHT.</head>
        <p>TOO MUCH LIGHT.</p>
        <p>A batch of people came before the magis- trates at the Borough Police Court on Tuesday charged with contraventions of the Lighting Order, and the following fines were inflicted : Frederick Dutton, 83, Padgate-lane, 55.; Robert Forrest, 42, Plumpton-street, 10s.; Mary Sauce, 1. Glass House-square, 55.; Dawson Bros., 59, Sankey-street (second offence), 205.; William Proffitt, 138, Church-street, 7s. 6d.; Mrs. Clarke, 108 a, Bridge-street, 10s.; Frank Dawson, 91, Thelwall-lane, 55.; Edward Kelly, 1, Carlisle- street, 55.; John Cann, Beresford-street, 10s.; Thos. Henry Harrison, 5, Allen-street, 2s. 6d.; John Holden, 35, Folly-lane, 55.; William Smith, 21, Norris-street, 55.; J. H. Teare, 34, Whitefleld- road (in respect of his work premises in Lyme. street), 10s.; Ernest Hanson, 16, Willis-street, ss. The following fines were inflicted at Thurs- day's Police Court :—John Humphries, 6, Jockey-street, 55.; Sarah Litlierland, 18, Eaton- street, 10s.-; A. E. Richardson, 59, Bridge-street, 10s.; Wm. Angus Boulting, Queen's Picture nhn Reedy, 8, 180, , BBilaacekkhhuurrsstt: •sPtarleeacte, , 5250.5;. ; Maryi z a b eAt street, 55.; George Shakeshaft, 2, Mersey- street, 10s.: Jog. Elwell. 227, Liverpool-road, 55..; Chas. Cook, Friars' Green House, Barbauld- street, ss.</p>
