        <p>Marriages. SELLEY—GORDOt the Parish Church, Preston, by special licence, John Selley, Army Pay Corps, son of John Selley, contractor, London, to Helen, daughter of John Gordon, 46, Arp street, Warrington. Deaths. BARLOW.—On October 9th, at 76, Laira-street, Sidney James Barlow, aged 6 years. HILL.—On October sth, at 16, Eustace-street, Prudence Emily Hill, aged 43 years. HITTSON.—On October sth, at 7, Jockey-street, Annie Hulson. aged 8 years. LYNCH.—On October 11th. at 1, Portland-street, Martin Lynch, aged 42 years. PARKES.—On October 11th, at 28, Bewsey-road, Joseph Parkes, aged 70 years. WOODS.—Richard Borrows Woods, at his resi- dence, "The Hales," Latchford. Funeral to-day (Saturday). Service at Stockton Heath Independ- ent Methodist Church at 2.0. Memorial Service Grappenhall Independent Methodist Church to- morrow (Sunday) evening at 6.0. lu Memoriam. DUTTON.—In loving memory of Henry Hewitt Dutton, who died October 11th, 1893. "To memory ever dear."</p>
