        <p>PRIVATE G. E. HALL. Wounded and Missing.</p>
        <p>DIED OF WOUNDS. PR IVATE D. M. MELVIN. Fateful News Arrives On His 24th Birthday. Mrs. A. Melvin, a widow-, who resides at 80. Longford-street, has received a letter written by Private Fred Hartley, of 24, Crosfield-street, saying that her son and only support, Private Donald McPherson Melvin, South Lancashire Regiment, had died of wounds. The letter says :—" Your son Donald was wounded near the shoulder by shrapnel. We were clearing a road when it happened. ' Don ' and myself being pals, I was with him when it happened. I carried him to a dressing station." Later a telegram arrived from the Record Office, Pres-</p>
